/-!
# The source seed normalizer in the linear-four branch

The natural marking makes N_H(V₃) a group with two-group kernel over a
subgroup of the binary plane parabolic. Its two-residual is generated by
cubics. Original 13.7.5 places those cubics in the literal point residual
L₁, and the original Sylow T supplements the two-residual. Consequently
N_H(V₃)=L₁T, with the original definitions and relative normalizers.

The critical-pair and terminal applications discharge the separate
seed-normalizer-control premise and obtain the seed order from the
original natural A₆ setup. They preserve the actual conjugator, quotient
maps and H_C/V_H sections. The natural and exterior markings, extra-line
movement and 13.8.31 chief obstruction remain unfinished obligations of
qt-d-138-linear-four-source. Earlier 13.8.27 remains with
qt-d-138-six-g2-source; final source assembly remains with qt-d-1381-source.
This is not a proof of the full 13.8.28 exclusion.

Source: Aschbacher--Smith, The Classification of Quasithin Groups,
combined manuscript of 1 March 2004, 13.7.5(3),13.8.32 and the proof
of 13.8.28, printed pp.938,965--966. The earlier 13.5.4(4) centralizer
bound and original maximal-local hypothesis enter through the proved
theta theorem, rather than through an assumed seed-normalizer conclusion.
-/

